            <ArticleTitle>Painful tonic spasms: an interesting phenomenon in cerebral ischemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>534-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of bilateral cerebral ischemia with frequent painful tonic spasms involving face, both upper and sometimes both lower extremities. The spasms subsided after treatment with diazepam.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
